{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_1d_inflow_right_upwind",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady 1-D linear advection u_t = -c D(u,x) + c dGdx on the unit interval [0, 1] with a prescribed inflow at the RIGHT wall, discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/upwind1_D_inflow_right_bc (1st-order FORWARD upwind interior, (gR-f[N])/dx inflow face). This is the sign-mirror of problems/advection_1d_inflow_upwind.esm (left inflow, backward upwind). SIGN CONVENTION: the forward-difference operator is upwind for flow in -x, so the transport speed is negative, c = -1; then the semi-discrete tendency -c D = +D = (f[i+1]-f[i])/dx is dissipative (Fourier growth rate Re[(exp(ik dx)-1)/dx] <= 0), the characteristics travel toward -x, and the domain INFLOW is the right wall x = 1 (outflow at the left wall x = 0). Manufactured STEADY solution u*(x) = cos(pi x) with the exactly matching steady forcing c dGdx, dGdx = g'(x) = -pi sin(pi x) (the analytic derivative of u*), so the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 and u(t) = u* for all t; the discrete field drifts only by the operator truncation error (forced-steady MMS: observed L2/Linf order = operator order = 1). INFLOW COMPATIBILITY (why cos(pi x) with gR = -1): the inflow value carried into the domain must equal the exact wall value, gR = u*(x=1) = cos(pi) = -1, and the manufactured profile must have g'(1) = 0 at the inflow wall. On this cell-centered grid the i=N face (gR-f[N])/dx approximates u*_x at x_N = 1 - dx/2; expanding, (u*(1) - u*(1-dx/2))/dx = (1/2) u*_x(1) + O(dx), so a nonzero wall gradient u*_x(1) would leave an O(1) boundary-cell residual that pollutes the observed order down toward 1/2 (a single O(1) cell contributes O(sqrt(dx)) to the normalized L2). cos(pi x) has u*_x = -pi sin(pi x) with u*_x(1) = 0 (and u*_x(0) = 0 at the outflow wall, which the forward stencil needs no closure for), so the inflow-cell residual is O(dx), consistent with the interior, and the global error is a clean O(dx). GRID CONTRACT WIRING (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0, 1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing by the metaparameter name N, substituted at load per esm-spec 9.7.6, so the convergence sweep's loader-API rebinding of N keeps dx consistent). gR is the rule's inflow free name, declared here as a parameter equal to the wall value; it lives only in the runtime rule body, never in a build-time ic/reference. The ic, the dGdx forcing, and the test references spell x_i = x0 + (i - 1/2) dx inline with load-foldable scalars (0 + (i - 1/2)(1/N)); the build-time 6.6.5/ic/observed cellwise evaluation is scope-free, so build-time coordinate expressions fold from literals and metaparameters alone (never the free-name x_coord template). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_inflow_right_upwind/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:problem", "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d", "equation:advection", "mms"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Section 4.8 (upwind methods) and Section 7 (inflow boundary conditions for advection)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Advection": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        { "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/upwind1_D_inflow_right_bc.esm" }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": ["x"],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the x index set."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": -1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed (non-positive; forward upwind for flow in -x). Multiplies both the discretized derivative and the manufactured forcing, so the steady MMS balance holds for any value; c = -1 makes -c D = +D dissipative and puts the inflow at the right wall."
        },
        "gR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": -1.0,
          "description": "Inflow value carried into the domain at the right wall x = x0 + N*dx (the rule's inflow free name). Set to the exact manufactured wall value u*(1) = cos(pi) = -1 so the boundary cell is consistent; a generic no-inflow consumer would leave the rule's default of 0."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "expression": { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] },
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "dGdx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "kg/m^4",
          "shape": ["x"],
          "description": "Analytic derivative of the manufactured solution: dGdx(x) = g'(x) = -pi sin(pi x). Constant in time; c dGdx is the manufactured forcing that holds u* = cos(pi x) steady. Cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N are spelled inline from literals and the metaparameter name N (build-time-foldable; never the free-name x_coord template).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i"],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                -3.141592653589793,
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "ic", "args": ["u"] },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "cos",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  3.141592653589793,
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": ["i"],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        0,
                        { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "t" },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  { "op": "-", "args": ["c"] },
                  { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "x" }
                ]
              },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["c", "dGdx"] }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_inflow_right_upwind",
          "description": "Manufactured steady solution u*(x) = cos(pi x) with c = -1 and right inflow gR = u*(1) = cos(pi) = -1. Derivation: the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 with u*_x = dGdx = -pi sin(pi x), so u(t) = u* exactly; the discrete drift is the pure 1st-order truncation of upwind1_D_inflow_right_bc, and -c D = +D is dissipative so the drift stays bounded. u*_x(1) = 0 makes the inflow-cell residual O(dx) (metadata.description), so the observed order is a clean 1. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.1 assertion bounds the truncation-driven drift against the SAME steady reference (well under the 0.05 bound at the default N=64, falling at order 1). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_inflow_right_upwind/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.1 },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": ["i"],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 0.05 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": ["i"],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
